# One hundred meshes — the case `AABound::get_bounding_box` is measured on.
#
# The same 948-triangle bunny instanced 100 times on a 10 x 10 grid. Nothing here is about the
# image: it exists because `get_bounding_box` on a `TriangleMesh` scans every vertex, so the number
# of times a build calls it only shows on a scene made of meshes. Four primitives hide it entirely,
# which is why every other scene in `test_files/` does.
#
# `bun_zipper_res4.ply` rather than the full bunny: the build cost per mesh is proportional to the
# vertex count and so is the PLY parse, so a bigger mesh raises both and changes nothing about what
# is visible. The grid step is 0.25, roughly twice the bunny's width, so the boxes do not overlap
# and the tree has something to separate.

camera pin_hole
  pos 1.2 0.8 1.6
  look 1.1 0.1 1.1
  up 0.0 1.0 0.0

scene
  object transformed
    object simple
      mesh file "test_files/bun_zipper_res4.ply"
      lambertian color 0.65 0.6 0.55
    transform { translate 0.00 0.0 0.00 }
  object transformed
    object simple
      mesh file "test_files/bun_zipper_res4.ply"
      lambertian color 0.65 0.6 0.55
    transform { translate 0.00 0.0 0.25 }
  object transformed
    object simple
      mesh file "test_files/bun_zipper_res4.ply"
      lambertian color 0.65 0.6 0.55
    transform { translate 0.00 0.0 0.50 }
  object transformed
